activation	Print prompt	2026-10-28T04:21:06.9815137Z {"title": "C API: expose function descriptions and positional parameter names to duckdb_functions()", "body": "`duckdb_functions()` can carry per-function `description`, `examples`, `categories` and named positional parameters, but only the **C++** registration path (`CreateTableFunctionInfo` / `CreateScalarFunctionInfo` + `FunctionDescription`) can populate them. The **C API** used by loadable extensions \u2014 including every Rust extension via `duckdb-rs` \u2014 has no equivalent:\n\n- `duckdb_table_function_add_parameter(tf, type)` takes only a type; there is no `duckdb_table_function_add_parameter(tf, name, type)`.\n- There is no `duckdb_*_set_description` for functions (the only such symbol is `duckdb_config_option_set_description`).\n- `duckdb_parameter_name` is for prepared-statement parameters, not function registration.\n\nConsequence: an extension built against the C API always shows `description = NULL`, `examples = []`, `categories = []`, and positional arguments as `col0, col1, \u2026` in `duckdb_functions()`. Agents and tools that discover extensions by querying `duckdb_functions()` (the only surface reachable from a SQL connection) therefore see nothing useful for these functions.\n\nVerified absent in `src/include/duckdb.h` / `duckdb_extension.h` on **v1.5.4, v1.5.5 and `main`**. The C++ side is handled (related: upstream reference  number 15876, which fixed `FunctionDescription`/named-parameter matching in `duckdb_functions.cpp`), but there is no C-API door to it.\n\n**Request:** add C-API setters mirroring `FunctionDescription` \u2014 description, examples, categories, and positional parameter names \u2014 for both `duckdb_table_function` and `duckdb_scalar_function`, and surface them in `duckdb_functions()`. \n\n**Why it matters here:** ~350 community extensions can only be discovered through `duckdb_functions()`; any built in Rust (or C) currently cannot document themselves at all through the supported registration path.\n"}
